Package: manifoldtest
Type: Package
Title: Independence Testing for Manifold-Valued Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Javier", "González-Delgado", email = "javiergonde@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for testing statistical independence between samples of
    manifold-valued data (currently the flat torus, e.g. angular or periodic
    measurements). Data are mapped from the manifold to a Euclidean
    tangent space via a
    logarithmic (inverse exponential) map at a chosen base point, optionally
    transformed to multidimensional ranks bounded in the unit ball via the
    center-outward distribution function of Hallin et al. (2021), and then
    tested for independence with the classical distance covariance test of
    Szekely, Rizzo and Bakirov (2007).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://gonzalez-delgado.github.io/manifoldtest/,
    https://github.com/gonzalez-delgado/manifoldtest
BugReports: https://github.com/gonzalez-delgado/manifoldtest/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    stats,
    transport,
    energy
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
